  "definition": "Involuntary hospitalization refers to an administrative scheme for making compulsory hospital admission decisions for offenders with mental disorder. In the source, it is discussed in the Japanese context as administrative involuntary hospitalization, where clinicians may need specific decision-making skills to determine when it is applied.",
